53	    /// The mesh <see cref="Indices"/> as 16-bit values, for rendering through the
54	    /// <c>short[]</c> overload of <c>DrawUserIndexedPrimitives</c>. Returns <c>null</c> when there
55	    /// are no indices, or when the mesh has more vertices than a 16-bit index can address
56	    /// (more than 65536) — in which case the caller must fall back to the 32-bit
57	    /// <see cref="Indices"/> (valid only on the HiDef profile).
58	    /// <para>
59	    /// Why: the overload's index-array type selects the GPU index width (<c>int[]</c> ⇒ 32-bit,
60	    /// <c>short[]</c> ⇒ 16-bit), and the Reach profile (WebGL ES2 / BlazorGL) rejects 32-bit
61	    /// indices with <c>"Reach profile does not support 32 bit indices"</c>. Procedural meshes are
